WEBVTT

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:45.660
We are dedicating this life-saving interest to the elder daughter, Victoria,

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:50.470
the bank and the castle called Green Fleet.

00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:54.470
With all the land and equipment, especially all the spears and valuables,

00:00:54.470 --> 00:01:00.000
which are deposited in the treasure of the castle, as verified in the application.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.850
and then they deprive their younger daughters of their real estate, all their building plots, their securities, their bank accounts.

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:37.300
Can't you look at your face or look at your fiancé?

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:41.480
You don't have to be afraid of the future.

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:44.690
You'll have enough of your fiancé.

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:53.080
Advocate Glenar. - Why are you smiling, Vicky?

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:54.940
I like you, Clara.

00:04:55.520 --> 00:05:00.000
Your character, your naive kindness and inexperience.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.190
You're my sister, but your face... it annoys me.

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:08.460
Victoria, please try at least a little more.

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:10.950
You'll see, you'll feel better for sure.

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:12.820
What do you know about that?

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:17.160
We're all different, but I don't want you to get upset and I don't.

00:05:17.720 --> 00:05:19.880
I'm glad I'm not the only one who thinks that.

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:25.270
Vicky, I like you as much as I like you.

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:27.880
We're sisters after all.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:29.350
All right, all right.

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:32.950
Let's not talk about it.

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:41.050
I wanted to ask you if you'd come with me to the Green Flat.

00:05:41.430 --> 00:05:54.260
When the house is being renovated, I don't feel very comfortable there.

00:05:55.350 --> 00:05:57.310
Isn't that your Green Flat?

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:00.000
Good night, then.

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:02.820
© BF-WATCH TV 2021

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:32.950
I've been drinking champagne for the whole week.

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:38.240
Caro, you're drunk again?

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:42.750
You'll break your stomach.

00:06:42.950 --> 00:06:48.330
Gerda, are the peasants here already?

00:06:48.530 --> 00:06:50.390
Yes, ma'am. They're setting up the tools.

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:55.710
I'll go talk to the master in a minute.

00:06:55.910 --> 00:06:59.090
They'll start in our rooms. We have to calm them down.

00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:00.000
It's so beautiful.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:04.340
I'm sorry, Vicky, but we won't have to deal with the Hara-Burdis.

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:09.870
Let them start making leisures and we'll have guests in the afternoon.

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:14.250
As you wish. It's about your house and your money.

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:22.630
- I just wanted to help you. - You're a good girl.

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:30.870
*BEEP*

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:34.560
*BEEP*

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:37.470
*BEEP*

00:07:37.470 --> 00:07:37.810
*BEEP*

00:08:06.430 --> 00:08:08.550
- Will you go to Venkov too? - I'll stay here.

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:11.590
- Klara's afraid of it. - What nonsense, Vicky!

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:16.430
- But yes, it's a dead dance floor. - What does the green girl in front of you belong to?

00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:20.900
- She walks around the halls and scares people. - Klara thinks about it, doesn't she?

00:08:21.380 --> 00:08:25.640
Vicky might overdo it, but it was cruel to die so young and beautiful.

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:30.000
And rich! It wasn't worth it anyway.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.850
Her lover went to the grave for her.

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:34.820
That's love!

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:38.440
He got a bad feeling for her.

00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:41.100
He was jealous of her love for dancing.

00:08:41.180 --> 00:08:44.620
He kissed her, but he wanted her only for himself.

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:47.170
Then he paid the doctors.

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:50.140
They told her she's dangerously ill

00:08:50.220 --> 00:08:53.990
and that she can't go out because her legs won't open.

00:08:54.070 --> 00:08:55.860
Come on, Clara!

00:08:55.940 --> 00:09:00.000
The informant saw her dancing for herself in front of the mirror.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:03.640
It's been a long time since she left home and then she got sick for real.

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:06.480
Excuse me, I'd like to tell you something, Clara.

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:07.920
Me too, Glennare.

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:10.420
Be so kind as to take care of your sister, yes.

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:12.240
You make me very happy.

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:20.250
Maybe she's not the most beautiful, but she's the most lovable of all.

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:22.080
Sometimes I even pour it myself.

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:29.860
That's why your shoes are so unnoticeable towards guests.

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:38.750
Don't sleep, sleep! Don't sleep!

00:09:48.560 --> 00:10:00.000
You won't lose your coat, will you? You won't be able to wear it for long.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:04.360
They didn't listen to us. - Yes, you see, ladies...

00:10:04.360 --> 00:10:17.840
Káro, I want to tell you something important.

00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:19.750
What happened to you?

00:10:19.750 --> 00:10:23.560
Nothing really. I wanted to write it to you, but I lost my courage.

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:29.440
And now... I should have written it to you sooner.

00:10:30.670 --> 00:10:32.670
Can I bring you a pencil and a paper?

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:36.180
Or would you rather say it?

00:10:37.940 --> 00:10:39.020
I wanted to be with you.

00:10:39.190 --> 00:10:41.790
- We've been together all afternoon. - But not alone.

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:43.660
Why aren't you used to it?

00:10:44.190 --> 00:10:46.190
I asked you to make it a company.

00:10:46.780 --> 00:10:48.260
I want to be with you.

00:10:48.860 --> 00:10:50.260
You don't understand.

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:53.110
You could have a little fun with it.

00:10:53.240 --> 00:10:55.840
Don't get angry, I don't like it.

00:10:56.620 --> 00:10:59.640
- At least you don't like it. - I like you.

00:11:00.250 --> 00:11:02.930
You see, you told me, and now it's better for you.

00:11:03.150 --> 00:11:05.470
Go back to your sister before I get too carried away, okay?

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:08.520
And come up with a friendly excuse why you disappeared.

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:23.330
Pussy, a foreign woman,

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:27.040
an unhappiness, death.

00:11:29.110 --> 00:11:30.000
A great wealth,

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:34.890
I see money and coins, all connected to the Black Lady.

00:11:34.970 --> 00:11:36.180
And that's you.

00:11:36.180 --> 00:11:40.010
Then there's money and wealth, all in your closeness.

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:46.340
On your way there's the Heart Lady, all in front of you.

00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:49.630
She's a threat to you. The Heart Lady.

00:11:49.650 --> 00:11:54.260
Go on.

00:11:54.260 --> 00:11:59.600
Then there's a priest. He turns around you.

00:12:00.410 --> 00:12:04.160
Then you'll wear a uniform, perhaps for love.

00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:07.590
But it's more for a lady with a heart.

00:12:08.800 --> 00:12:13.160
- The one that bothers me? - Yes, but it's up to you

00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:18.630
to get rid of the obstacle between you and wealth.

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:24.840
Then there's the road, perhaps for misfortune.

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:28.100
That's enough.

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:21.220
So, Jano, you mustn't oil it.

00:13:21.220 --> 00:13:26.150
You won't feel anything anyway.

00:13:26.150 --> 00:13:30.000
You would just slowly sink, sink...

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:33.870
...until you fell asleep forever.

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:37.830
And no one would know why.

00:13:37.830 --> 00:13:47.550
Do you hear that?

00:13:47.550 --> 00:13:51.010
Our little rose.

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:54.770
Nice, isn't it? But chopped flowers smell better.

00:14:01.530 --> 00:14:10.530
We'll be glad to have her, yes. We'll remember her with love.

00:15:09.820 --> 00:15:14.120
I want to start the restoration work from this side, from my room.

00:15:14.120 --> 00:15:15.570
Yes, I'll tell them right away.

00:15:15.570 --> 00:15:18.500
I'm leaving, so I won't disturb anyone here.

00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:42.680
I'm sorry.

00:17:04.570 --> 00:17:24.480
I thought you were up.

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:26.780
Vicky, have breakfast with me.

00:17:26.780 --> 00:17:29.060
Thank you, I've already eaten.

00:17:31.560 --> 00:17:33.710
Call the leader, Klara.

00:17:33.710 --> 00:17:37.190
Let him send us a copy of the carpet. It's been a week.

00:17:37.190 --> 00:17:41.450
I'll be done in a minute. Or call him yourself.

00:17:41.450 --> 00:17:46.540
You know I'd like to talk to him.

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:56.900
I'd like to call 38.

00:17:56.900 --> 00:17:58.130
Yes, I'll wait.

00:18:02.620 --> 00:18:09.360
Shouldn't I call later? No one's picking up.

00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:29.060
Just a moment. Wait. What did the singer say?

00:18:30.320 --> 00:18:40.640
They put me together badly. I'll try it again in a moment.

00:18:40.640 --> 00:18:43.760
It was foamy a while ago. Now it's like it's dead.

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:46.760
Well, dead water. It's like from a fairy tale.

00:18:46.760 --> 00:18:52.880
It's been like that for a long time. Káro, have some cocoa and then we'll have a new one.

00:18:52.880 --> 00:18:56.920
I'm starving.

00:19:05.470 --> 00:19:07.460
I'd rather smoke less.

00:19:11.900 --> 00:19:16.310
You're so funny. - What's gotten into you?

00:19:17.270 --> 00:19:18.720
You won't laugh.

00:19:19.870 --> 00:19:25.290
I could smoke more eggs, so I could take lots of other eggs.

00:19:25.450 --> 00:19:30.000
But I don't want to eat them all. - You need to drink so many eggs.

00:19:44.680 --> 00:19:49.490
When I leave, you'll be happy, won't you, Vicky?

00:19:49.570 --> 00:19:52.500
That's just the way it is.

00:20:19.130 --> 00:20:22.150
Come and see us sometime, it's really close by.

00:20:22.310 --> 00:20:30.000
I'll visit you too. - We'll figure it out later.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:44.080
I'll write it down here. Bye. - Bye.

00:21:32.430 --> 00:22:00.000
It's clear. He's possessed, as always. At least I know I'm at home.

00:22:00.760 --> 00:22:02.850
Keep an eye out for the windows.

00:22:03.990 --> 00:22:05.990
You'll be calling me every week.

00:22:06.150 --> 00:22:08.260
As you wish, Your Honor.

00:22:08.490 --> 00:22:11.210
I'd like to make a decision, Your Honor.

00:22:11.370 --> 00:22:15.200
The old barn in the courtyard should be demolished.

00:22:15.260 --> 00:22:17.860
I forbade you to plant flowers here.

00:22:18.680 --> 00:22:20.420
And don't bring them to my room.

00:22:22.070 --> 00:22:23.880
Thank you. You may go.

00:22:31.820 --> 00:22:32.980
Georgiano.

00:23:42.280 --> 00:23:44.240
It's over between us now, isn't it?

00:23:44.240 --> 00:23:51.350
I'm afraid they would take us and sell us ordinary water.

00:24:06.650 --> 00:24:10.380
Nelly, is that the dog that our sister found?

00:24:10.380 --> 00:24:13.480
Yes, he grew up that time. They take him out with his son all day.

00:24:52.520 --> 00:24:55.840
They've brought a new sewing machine. I didn't want to buy it before...

00:24:55.920 --> 00:24:56.920
I'll be right there.

00:25:30.440 --> 00:25:32.440
I still have a terrible cold.

00:25:33.580 --> 00:25:35.030
I'm sure it'll be fine.

00:25:35.740 --> 00:25:37.780
No, I'll call you.

00:25:38.450 --> 00:25:40.120
Have a good time.

00:25:48.640 --> 00:25:59.120
Bring me the lemonade again.

00:26:12.060 --> 00:26:15.910
Gordo, look, don't I have a wide-open eye?

00:26:15.910 --> 00:26:21.170
I don't see anything, miss, it's just your vision.

00:26:21.170 --> 00:26:23.560
But my lips are swollen.

00:26:30.120 --> 00:26:33.400
- They're not oranges. - They're the same as always.

00:26:36.250 --> 00:26:50.250
I'm glad you came. There are only a few people here.

00:26:50.330 --> 00:26:53.720
- You're still a little pale. - Give me something to drink, please.

00:26:53.880 --> 00:26:57.680
- What would you like? - A lot of water.

00:27:07.770 --> 00:27:13.240
I don't feel any pain, I just feel as if someone had changed my whole body.

00:27:17.080 --> 00:27:20.680
Now you can rest when Viktoria leaves, and you'll be home alone.

00:27:40.400 --> 00:27:41.840
Were you scared a lot?

00:27:43.110 --> 00:27:44.210
It was strange.

00:27:45.100 --> 00:27:52.650
It was as if the depth suddenly closed its mouth.

00:27:55.040 --> 00:27:56.640
I couldn't move.

00:27:57.100 --> 00:28:00.000
I had to look down as if something was pulling me.

00:28:15.040 --> 00:28:19.520
She saved me from death.

00:28:19.520 --> 00:28:21.820
I was almost overtaken by a locomotive.

00:28:21.820 --> 00:28:25.120
I have no idea how it passed me.

00:28:25.120 --> 00:28:27.120
Maybe I was overtaken by a locomotive.

00:28:27.120 --> 00:28:30.000
I saved myself, however, instinctively.

00:28:30.090 --> 00:28:34.530
but I never got used to the movement I saved myself with.

00:28:35.480 --> 00:28:38.770
Sorry, but I can also say something about that adventure with the bat.

00:28:38.770 --> 00:28:42.160
One moment, please.

00:28:42.160 --> 00:28:45.810
Our connection is a little strange.

00:28:45.810 --> 00:28:49.410
And this is a distant cousin, Lieutenant Marek.

00:28:49.410 --> 00:28:52.880
Last week he was taken to the local camp.

00:29:00.830 --> 00:29:05.500
-Who found him? -I was riding a horse down the river.

00:29:06.040 --> 00:29:11.400
He was lying on the shore, under the rock.

00:29:12.300 --> 00:29:13.760
Like in a novel, right?

00:31:14.430 --> 00:31:17.630
You know, there are a lot of diseases that start as a counter-indicator

00:31:17.630 --> 00:31:20.240
and that appear later.

00:31:20.240 --> 00:31:23.440
So, we have to wait?

00:31:23.440 --> 00:31:27.280
Yes. Do you miss anything?

00:31:27.280 --> 00:31:30.000
Take a novel or read a book.

00:31:30.030 --> 00:31:33.730
And don't forget to use chinin for safety.

00:31:33.730 --> 00:31:37.290
Malaria has various hidden forms.

00:31:37.290 --> 00:31:41.200
But where would you get malaria, right?

00:31:41.200 --> 00:31:43.790
But use it for safety.

00:31:43.790 --> 00:31:55.460
And, of course, diet. It's important here.

00:31:55.460 --> 00:31:58.150
The house is being repaired.

00:32:11.480 --> 00:32:14.280
Excuse me, Miss, I've brought the new carpet patterns.

00:32:15.440 --> 00:32:17.160
Hasn't my sister sent you a message?

00:32:17.740 --> 00:32:20.200
I didn't see her. They told me she was sick.

00:32:21.940 --> 00:32:23.080
What did they say about her?

00:32:23.360 --> 00:32:26.640
The doctor doesn't know. She only wants to drink.

00:32:26.840 --> 00:32:30.000
- And she's very weak. - To drink?

00:32:31.720 --> 00:32:33.720
We'll give him something to drink.

00:32:33.720 --> 00:32:39.860
Wait, there's nothing there.

00:32:39.860 --> 00:32:41.950
We'll give him something to drink.

00:32:41.950 --> 00:32:56.370
I'd like a cup of tea, please.

00:32:56.370 --> 00:32:59.730
You forgot about the window again.

00:33:00.280 --> 00:33:03.910
I'm sorry, please. We leave them open because of the cat.

00:33:04.550 --> 00:33:07.970
He always comes back. - He'll kill me.

00:33:14.210 --> 00:33:18.850
Wait, Nelly. Take the glass away.

00:33:20.160 --> 00:33:25.830
I'll drink tea from the cup. - You'll always give me a cup.

00:37:53.770 --> 00:37:54.640
You can go now.

00:40:31.470 --> 00:40:33.070
His chest is injured.

00:40:36.580 --> 00:40:39.300
The doctor says he may never be able to move his head again.

00:40:41.170 --> 00:41:00.000
He can't eat. Take it away from that girl.

00:41:00.000 --> 00:41:02.560
It's a gift from the Lord.

00:41:02.560 --> 00:41:06.360
What are you doing?

00:41:06.360 --> 00:41:07.840
He's still playing.

00:41:07.840 --> 00:41:10.630
He drank milk from his bowl.

00:41:10.630 --> 00:41:13.430
Mom, can I eat it?

00:41:13.430 --> 00:41:16.290
He's a little hot. I'll put it in the bed.

00:41:53.550 --> 00:41:58.640
This is your house. You live in solitude.

00:42:00.890 --> 00:42:05.610
Don't worry, I'm careful. I've just reached the bridge, I'm on foot.

00:42:06.630 --> 00:42:14.440
I can sit down. - Please, what would you like?

00:42:16.410 --> 00:42:21.270
Listen, I'm here to find out.

00:42:23.680 --> 00:42:28.030
You'll find out for yourself.

00:42:31.050 --> 00:42:32.150
Nothing has happened yet.

00:42:32.410 --> 00:42:34.110
But you got the reinforcement.

00:42:34.370 --> 00:42:34.890
Yes.

00:42:35.980 --> 00:42:36.580
Excellent.

00:42:38.240 --> 00:42:40.140
Are you waiting for a natural situation, or...

00:42:40.140 --> 00:42:43.640
You've assured me that you don't interfere with the interests of your clients.

00:42:44.470 --> 00:42:45.070
I hope...

00:42:45.170 --> 00:42:45.970
Let's talk about things.

00:42:46.450 --> 00:42:48.050
Your sister has a congenital tumor.

00:42:48.570 --> 00:42:53.920
It is treated by Dr. Meyer, who recently told one of his friends that your sister's disease is...

00:42:54.690 --> 00:42:57.790
that your sister's disease is at least very strange.

00:42:59.220 --> 00:43:00.000
Do you have an X-ray?

00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:06.970
My sister's illness is nothing but a normal indifference.

00:43:07.090 --> 00:43:09.790
Your order was very precise.

00:43:09.910 --> 00:43:12.630
You wanted her to drink slowly, so that the one who drank it

00:43:12.750 --> 00:43:15.710
would die after a while, before she could find out the cause.

00:43:15.830 --> 00:43:17.750
Your words are very precise.

00:43:17.870 --> 00:43:22.350
You wanted a liquid without taste and smell that should not be stored.

00:43:22.470 --> 00:43:24.690
Not even in the laboratory.

00:43:24.810 --> 00:43:28.500
- Is that so? - I don't understand.

00:43:28.620 --> 00:43:30.000
I understand.

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:35.110
Your order was difficult and the production was very complicated.

00:43:35.470 --> 00:43:38.140
We had to make a lot of attempts

00:43:38.500 --> 00:43:42.700
and we had high sales, a higher price than the paid one.

00:43:42.900 --> 00:43:47.230
You're rich, you'll inherit the sisterhood.

00:43:47.350 --> 00:43:50.080
I think we'll make an agreement.

00:43:50.200 --> 00:43:51.710
That's very kind of you.

00:43:51.830 --> 00:44:00.000
Can you imagine how your sister would feel?

00:44:00.030 --> 00:44:04.460
I've read a letter with some interesting information.

00:44:05.740 --> 00:44:08.250
But you sold me the bottle.

00:44:10.010 --> 00:44:12.650
I have evidence that you stole the bottle from Jeda's chest

00:44:12.730 --> 00:44:15.570
when my husband showed it to you and told you about its properties.

00:44:17.160 --> 00:44:19.360
Don't you remember how the maid caught you

00:44:19.440 --> 00:44:21.500
when you were getting off at Jeda's chest?

00:44:27.370 --> 00:44:30.000
You've got it all wrong.

00:44:31.470 --> 00:44:34.370
It's not meant for my sister. - You're ridiculous.

00:44:34.850 --> 00:44:38.900
She's my sister, for God's sake. - I'm listening.

00:44:40.760 --> 00:44:43.850
Please, I'll give you some money voluntarily.

00:44:44.730 --> 00:44:47.970
I'll go to the city, to the bank and visit your husband.

00:44:48.050 --> 00:44:49.490
I'll take the money from him. - Don't bother my husband.

00:44:49.570 --> 00:44:52.290
He's a scientist, he doesn't care. I'll take the money.

00:44:53.150 --> 00:44:59.060
How much? - You'll get five thousand.

00:45:03.320 --> 00:45:05.640
So that's the price for your letters to the criminal?

00:45:05.640 --> 00:45:14.930
So you think you can grab all the money and then disappear somewhere

00:45:14.930 --> 00:45:17.330
so you can use it unknowingly?

00:45:18.380 --> 00:45:18.880
Hm.

00:45:20.000 --> 00:45:22.900
Or do you want to look for a guy you'd put gold on his eyes

00:45:22.900 --> 00:45:25.060
so he wouldn't see your ugly anger?

00:45:25.060 --> 00:45:28.320
But why do you want to save on me?

00:45:31.440 --> 00:45:35.400
I can still come to your sister and tell her how she's recovering.

00:45:36.280 --> 00:45:39.940
That's the end of all plans.

00:45:41.360 --> 00:45:48.210
Come on. - Please, let Gerda bring me the paper.

00:45:48.260 --> 00:45:52.180
Is it necessary? - Calm down. That's the best.

00:45:52.430 --> 00:45:54.420
I'd like to write to my sister.

00:45:54.990 --> 00:46:00.000
I hoped it would work out, but now...

00:46:05.210 --> 00:46:07.430
What kind of a doctor? I didn't understand your name.

00:46:07.430 --> 00:46:21.290
I just wanted to know.

00:46:23.370 --> 00:46:28.200
I have cancer, tuberculosis, blood and brain hallucinations.

00:46:30.060 --> 00:46:31.830
at least according to the medical books.

00:47:35.980 --> 00:47:38.750
Don't worry, your sister is poisoned to death.

00:47:39.360 --> 00:47:41.370
Even if I can cure her.

00:47:42.570 --> 00:47:45.280
Does the doctor have a choice? - No.

00:47:45.690 --> 00:47:47.800
He doesn't know how to eat, so he can't use antibiotics.

00:47:48.730 --> 00:47:53.310
How much? - 500,000 CZK.

00:47:55.540 --> 00:47:57.080
500,000 CZK?

00:48:01.080 --> 00:48:05.010
500,000.

00:48:09.520 --> 00:48:10.950
Seems like the names are right.

00:48:11.700 --> 00:48:13.750
Some of them are quite nice.

00:48:15.260 --> 00:48:17.440
But most of them are of the worst quality.

00:48:17.520 --> 00:48:19.560
Those pearls are made of glass. Do you have anything else?

00:48:21.260 --> 00:48:29.690
But you'll only get what's on the table.

00:48:31.020 --> 00:48:36.840
The bottle is untouched. You can see it whenever you want.

00:48:37.680 --> 00:48:40.460
- Do you promise? - I'll show you the bottle.

00:48:40.820 --> 00:48:41.810
Show me, dear.

00:48:45.040 --> 00:48:48.840
I'll show you that in the bottle is only what you poured the poison in.

00:48:49.870 --> 00:48:54.990
- You'd have to unpack the package. - What do you mean?

00:48:55.480 --> 00:49:00.000
I haven't unpacked it. Maybe I'm stupid, but I got a call

00:49:00.000 --> 00:49:02.400
I was afraid everyone would know about him.

00:49:03.400 --> 00:49:07.610
I hid him in various places.

00:49:08.610 --> 00:49:12.440
Every night I got up to make sure no one had stolen him.

00:49:13.440 --> 00:49:17.250
In the end, I rather buried him here,

00:49:19.490 --> 00:49:22.810
near my house, in the rocks, above the cliff.

00:49:38.220 --> 00:49:43.330
All right, show me the package and I'll take it back.

00:49:43.910 --> 00:49:46.170
Why? Is it enough that I told you?

00:49:48.550 --> 00:49:52.840
No, it's not.

00:49:57.180 --> 00:49:58.760
Thank you very much for the money.

00:49:58.860 --> 00:50:00.000
It's nothing.

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:01.280
Get well soon.

00:50:46.600 --> 00:50:49.360
Wait! - Do you think I'm lying?

00:50:49.600 --> 00:50:53.090
Maybe you forgot about the place.

00:50:54.500 --> 00:50:56.120
Don't worry, it's not far.

00:51:00.190 --> 00:51:11.490
I won't go any further. Wait a second, we're almost there.

00:51:31.400 --> 00:51:42.890
It's easy to make a mess. Come here, Vitek. Try it.

00:51:47.800 --> 00:51:59.060
Yes. - Try it.

00:52:01.760 --> 00:52:03.200
I don't know.

00:54:06.330 --> 00:54:08.530
Are you up again? You know it's forbidden.

00:54:08.610 --> 00:54:11.890
I hope the doctor doesn't find out I was in the garden for five minutes.

00:54:12.420 --> 00:54:14.600
You can't kill me. You know how much it hurts.

00:54:18.150 --> 00:54:25.990
I'll be right back. I feel better now.

00:54:26.550 --> 00:54:28.840
I'll tell the doctor.

00:56:13.600 --> 00:56:17.570
- What's your name? - Clara, I know.

00:56:19.390 --> 00:56:21.880
I'm ill, you know.

00:56:22.260 --> 00:56:27.910
You don't know who I am yet. We're very similar. You're my sister.

00:56:30.000 --> 00:56:35.340
I don't have anyone. Please...

00:56:35.540 --> 00:56:41.810
What's wrong with you?

00:56:42.010 --> 00:56:44.840
Let me go, please. You've driven her away.

00:56:45.640 --> 00:56:48.660
I need your help. You know I love you.

00:56:48.870 --> 00:56:50.070
No, let me go.

00:56:51.070 --> 00:57:00.000
I'll report your misdeeds to the police.

00:57:00.540 --> 00:57:05.410
It's my fault. - Let me decide for myself.

00:57:05.610 --> 00:57:11.930
Who's to blame? Why is there a noise?

00:57:12.130 --> 00:57:16.070
Get out of here! The patient needs an ambulance!

00:57:16.270 --> 00:57:25.070
You're weak, but you're right. What do you think?

00:57:25.270 --> 00:57:28.090
I don't know. - What?

00:57:30.000 --> 00:57:31.960
It's called hallucination, isn't it?

00:57:33.440 --> 00:57:35.250
Hallucination?

00:57:36.300 --> 00:57:37.300
You don't smoke hashish, do you?

00:57:38.830 --> 00:57:40.360
Something has affected your nervous system.

00:57:41.360 --> 00:57:43.190
That's why the light, sounds and colours bother you.

00:57:44.200 --> 00:57:46.400
Show me.

00:57:49.880 --> 00:57:50.880
Your organs are fine.

00:57:52.530 --> 00:57:53.530
Maybe it's the liver, according to the map.

00:57:54.960 --> 00:57:55.960
But it's not so pink that I could find it.

00:57:56.910 --> 00:57:57.910
If there are any changes,

00:57:59.280 --> 00:58:00.000
better or worse,

00:58:00.000 --> 00:58:03.970
I'll call for a counsellor.

00:58:04.050 --> 00:58:07.330
Don't be afraid. We have more cases like this than you think.

00:58:07.410 --> 00:58:08.750
See?

00:58:10.060 --> 00:58:15.480
In any case, lie down. You can't damage anything.

00:58:15.560 --> 00:58:17.530
I'll be back tomorrow.

00:58:17.750 --> 00:58:21.880
Doctor, tell me I won't die.

00:58:21.960 --> 00:58:26.160
Fear won't help.

00:58:26.240 --> 00:58:28.450
And listen to the nurse.

00:58:32.360 --> 00:58:36.240
- What about your boy? - It's nothing.

00:58:36.460 --> 00:58:39.830
He's flying with the dog again.

00:59:02.680 --> 00:59:04.680
Morgano.

01:00:57.640 --> 01:00:58.290
- Dream doll?

01:01:00.030 --> 01:01:02.950
Vicky, I'm glad you're here.

01:01:04.370 --> 01:01:06.570
This is Marik Příbuzný and Vyhornové.

01:01:06.650 --> 01:01:09.060
We met at her place.

01:01:11.850 --> 01:01:14.460
What's the matter, doctor?

01:01:14.540 --> 01:01:17.930
I think she doesn't know what's wrong with me.

01:01:18.180 --> 01:01:20.450
How are you doing in your room, Vicky?

01:01:20.540 --> 01:01:22.410
It's quiet there.

01:01:22.830 --> 01:01:25.640
If only she'd change immediately

01:01:25.790 --> 01:01:28.310
after that crazy idea of yours with the labours.

01:01:28.460 --> 01:01:29.280
You think...

01:01:30.000 --> 01:01:33.470
There are so many diseases that doctors don't know yet.

01:01:33.550 --> 01:01:35.550
Excuse me. - Maročka?

01:01:35.630 --> 01:01:46.360
No, I'm still having nightmares.

01:01:46.440 --> 01:01:50.540
I can't sleep. The doctor wants to call an ambulance.

01:01:50.620 --> 01:01:54.840
Mr. Poručík wants to learn how to fly an aeroplane.

01:01:54.920 --> 01:01:57.930
The aeroplanes are falling, and the pilots are dying.

01:01:58.010 --> 01:02:00.000
The aeroplane is falling, and the pilots are dying.

01:02:02.620 --> 01:02:06.400
Most of them are still young, after all.

01:02:06.530 --> 01:02:10.840
Isn't it wonderful to die in Prague as an adult?

01:02:12.730 --> 01:02:17.470
Thank you. I don't wish to die. I'll wait for my old age.

01:02:18.940 --> 01:02:21.570
Please, sir, listen to me.

01:02:31.280 --> 01:02:39.960
What's with you, Vicky? - What's with me? What's with you, I wonder?

01:02:41.880 --> 01:02:48.260
I don't know. I'm probably mad, Vicky. I've got bad thoughts.

01:02:48.580 --> 01:02:51.910
I'll tell you when I'm well.

01:02:51.990 --> 01:02:56.660
Of course, of course. You mustn't get mad now.

01:02:57.820 --> 01:03:00.000
They're beautiful.

01:03:01.280 --> 01:03:03.240
Do you have a free bandage?

01:03:03.590 --> 01:03:06.050
You get a lot of them, don't you?

01:03:07.120 --> 01:03:10.280
We can throw out the worst ones from Mr. Glénar's notary.

01:03:10.850 --> 01:03:12.580
I think you've had enough, ma'am.

01:03:12.590 --> 01:03:14.150
I'll see to Mr. Poručík.

01:03:16.220 --> 01:03:18.630
Mr. Poručík? - Yes?

01:03:30.410 --> 01:03:34.150
You have a good influence on Clara, don't you?

01:03:35.740 --> 01:03:40.410
A strange change, but I'm sure she'll get better.

01:03:41.330 --> 01:03:44.130
So you're still optimistic about her illness?

01:03:44.660 --> 01:03:46.060
I think you love her.

01:03:46.860 --> 01:03:48.780
I don't know what's to do with her illness.

01:03:49.260 --> 01:03:50.740
But, child, of course not.

01:03:52.070 --> 01:03:55.470
But I think you'd like a lot of suffering and hindrance.

01:03:55.550 --> 01:03:56.990
You want to suffer a lot, don't you?

01:03:58.600 --> 01:04:00.000
If you had a son,

01:04:00.000 --> 01:04:02.400
Or would you rather save his life?

01:04:02.400 --> 01:04:05.220
Clara could thank you then,

01:04:05.220 --> 01:04:09.000
so you could put your pain to rest with a smile.

01:04:09.000 --> 01:04:11.320
Is that right, Marko?

01:04:11.320 --> 01:04:18.930
I can tell you that.

01:04:18.930 --> 01:04:23.700
It really is so.

01:04:23.700 --> 01:04:27.620
Almost exactly.

01:05:03.200 --> 01:05:07.080
My Viktorka. Where did you find her?

01:05:07.870 --> 01:05:09.960
In the barn that Gerda took from the floor.

01:05:10.200 --> 01:05:11.600
Wasn't your Klara there?

01:05:12.000 --> 01:05:14.160
She was completely faint and had no eyes left.

01:05:17.360 --> 01:05:22.970
Klara, I have to tell you something.

01:05:23.590 --> 01:05:30.000
No, first listen to me, Vik. You have to forgive me.

01:05:30.000 --> 01:05:37.590
I'm sorry I couldn't think of it, but now, when I'm not a father any more,

01:05:37.590 --> 01:05:40.790
I have only you. When I'm healthy, I think I'll give up.

01:05:40.790 --> 01:05:47.730
Mark hasn't told me anything yet, but I know he loves me, and I like him.

01:05:47.730 --> 01:05:49.970
Then I'll be useless.

01:05:49.970 --> 01:06:00.000
No, you mustn't say that. You'll stay with me, with us, and you'll go nowhere.

01:06:00.000 --> 01:06:02.990
We both will like you. - Of course, of course.

01:06:03.310 --> 01:06:08.200
But you wanted to tell me something. I didn't even let you speak.

01:06:08.560 --> 01:06:11.780
But no, it wasn't so important.

01:06:12.100 --> 01:06:18.260
Nothing at all. Actually, it's just a feeling.

01:06:20.290 --> 01:06:23.870
You see, we haven't talked like this for a long time.

01:06:24.190 --> 01:06:30.000
I like it right away. I like you.

01:06:33.360 --> 01:06:36.740
That's not bluffing. That's just provocation.

01:06:36.820 --> 01:06:39.890
To hold a stupid card like that and to win over her.

01:06:40.210 --> 01:06:42.610
That's the last thing I let you do.

01:06:44.330 --> 01:06:49.520
Yesterday you said honestly that you wouldn't like it at all.

01:07:38.730 --> 01:07:42.760
Well, gentlemen, and now all of you, for all of you.

01:07:43.180 --> 01:07:44.690
Who has it? And I'll give it to you.

01:07:45.450 --> 01:07:46.640
I have it.

01:07:46.880 --> 01:07:49.720
Here you go. But I don't have it anymore.

01:08:42.990 --> 01:08:43.890
What are you doing?

01:11:37.770 --> 01:11:42.410
Where are you going at night? - Why are you running away from me?

01:11:42.410 --> 01:11:48.200
Do you want to talk to me? Have you written the letter?

01:11:48.200 --> 01:11:52.880
Yes, I've written it to you. I've written it a few times, but...

01:11:52.880 --> 01:11:54.910
Go away. - Clara...

01:11:56.120 --> 01:12:00.000
Let me go. - Listen to me. You're ill. I want to help you.

01:12:00.730 --> 01:12:02.730
Let me go, you son of a bitch!

01:12:07.570 --> 01:12:10.150
She didn't eat anything when you left for town.

01:12:11.340 --> 01:12:12.560
All she did was drink.

01:12:13.240 --> 01:12:19.230
And she's been lying here since last night.

01:12:20.490 --> 01:12:23.310
Take her away.

01:12:25.280 --> 01:12:26.080
It's over.

01:12:33.580 --> 01:12:34.520
That's right!

01:14:31.440 --> 01:14:32.680
They're not sleeping yet.

01:14:32.680 --> 01:14:35.020
Of course they're not sleeping, they have to get ready.

01:14:35.020 --> 01:14:37.580
If they were sleeping, they wouldn't have to get up from their beds.

01:14:37.580 --> 01:14:39.030
Ladies!

01:15:19.960 --> 01:15:20.930
I'll do it.

01:16:19.520 --> 01:16:27.910
It's nothing. Everything's fine. - You don't like me, do you?

01:16:30.190 --> 01:16:35.750
You're so sweet, but don't get angry, I don't want to.

01:16:35.800 --> 01:16:44.940
Mr. Officer is probably used to younger people, isn't he?

01:16:45.020 --> 01:16:50.290
And she's a musician.

01:16:51.510 --> 01:16:54.090
You can only ruin everything.

01:17:02.430 --> 01:17:09.350
Oh, you mustn't hurt her or she'll run away.

01:17:12.670 --> 01:17:14.440
Come on, come here.

01:17:17.800 --> 01:17:20.740
Go to the hut. I already told you she's not here.

01:17:20.900 --> 01:17:22.760
You're lying. The cat is waiting here.

01:17:23.520 --> 01:17:25.360
Tell him I have to talk to the butcher.

01:17:26.280 --> 01:17:27.140
Go!

01:17:39.400 --> 01:17:42.420
Why did they bring you here? Get out!

01:18:00.000 --> 01:18:07.560
I want him to drag me out, or I'll cut his neck off!

01:18:09.440 --> 01:18:10.780
What are you looking at?

01:18:11.070 --> 01:18:17.840
He's waiting for you, so he can get you out of trouble.

01:18:18.510 --> 01:18:20.790
At least I don't have to talk to you.

01:18:20.870 --> 01:18:23.070
I think we've taken over his girl.

01:18:26.230 --> 01:18:27.750
He'll get your Clara.

01:18:33.360 --> 01:18:37.680
I heard about you from Mrs. Klára. You don't have to explain anything to me.

01:18:37.760 --> 01:18:39.240
It's a simple situation.

01:18:39.320 --> 01:18:42.920
I'm here for work. My friends are inside. I can call them witnesses.

01:18:43.000 --> 01:18:46.600
- Pick up the gun, please. - But that's stupid.

01:18:46.680 --> 01:18:49.070
- Sir! - What is it? Should I break his mouth?

01:18:49.150 --> 01:18:52.520
- I didn't come to beat you. - You didn't come to beat me, but you can beat me.

01:18:52.600 --> 01:18:56.460
- Listen! - Klára left the house last night.

01:18:56.540 --> 01:19:00.000
You know about her illness. She was looking for you in the casino.

01:19:00.000 --> 01:19:02.720
I thought you should know it. - Thank you.

01:19:02.800 --> 01:19:05.840
Where are you going, mate? Without us?

01:19:05.920 --> 01:19:09.320
Wait, wait. You were drinking with us, you were playing with us.

01:19:09.320 --> 01:19:11.980
You're going to the pub with us again.

01:19:24.570 --> 01:19:27.140
I'm going to the pub with you.

01:19:42.090 --> 01:19:44.860
The note was written by a fortune teller, and you ran off with it.

01:19:44.860 --> 01:19:46.500
Give me back the note.

01:19:46.500 --> 01:19:47.550
Vicky!

01:19:47.550 --> 01:19:52.430
You shouldn't have. Why did you poison me?

01:19:52.430 --> 01:19:55.990
What, do you really think I'm rude?

01:19:55.990 --> 01:19:57.940
You've been loving me since the morning.

01:19:57.940 --> 01:19:58.680
Viktoria.

01:20:01.180 --> 01:20:05.640
Please tell me the truth. I want to know the truth.

01:20:06.030 --> 01:20:10.030
I don't know anything. Leave me alone.

01:20:10.210 --> 01:20:20.590
All right. I'll ask that person to come and tell me everything.

01:20:22.110 --> 01:20:26.860
I'll pay whatever he wants, but I'll know the truth.

01:20:29.080 --> 01:20:30.000
Are you crazy?

01:20:30.090 --> 01:20:33.330
I want to know how my sister killed me.

01:20:33.620 --> 01:20:36.150
Shut up! I don't want to hear anything.

01:20:37.850 --> 01:20:39.600
You're sick, you hear me?

01:20:39.770 --> 01:20:41.490
Yes, you're right, I'm sick.

01:20:42.510 --> 01:20:46.020
I just want to know why you did it. Tell me the truth.

01:20:46.250 --> 01:20:51.110
The truth! - I'll tell you.

01:20:53.820 --> 01:21:00.000
I bought... I bought...

01:21:02.810 --> 01:21:12.780
from... from some kind of...

01:21:13.230 --> 01:21:16.130
some kind of strange water

01:21:18.060 --> 01:21:19.880
that I'm supposed to call "strange dreams".

01:21:21.180 --> 01:21:23.010
Are you tired? I'll cut it short.

01:21:25.540 --> 01:21:29.700
I'm done. Oh. Yes.

01:21:31.240 --> 01:21:35.310
Secretly, so you wouldn't know, I gave you a few drops.

01:21:36.340 --> 01:21:39.640
You bought them for yourself and gave them to me.

01:21:43.050 --> 01:21:45.200
I wanted to see the effect. - On me?

01:21:46.580 --> 01:21:50.870
Why not? You like to talk about your dreams so much.

01:21:51.950 --> 01:21:54.550
I didn't think I could hurt you.

01:21:55.900 --> 01:21:59.190
I just wanted to make you happy. - Yes.

01:22:00.160 --> 01:22:08.530
I was hoping you'd tell me about dreams that never happened to you.

01:22:22.760 --> 01:22:26.880
Now I see I got into the hands of nothing.

01:22:27.930 --> 01:22:30.000
They sold me something harmful

01:22:30.000 --> 01:22:31.840
They couldn't have taken the money from me.

01:22:31.920 --> 01:22:34.800
They couldn't have known that you'd give me the money?

01:22:37.600 --> 01:22:43.690
Actually, yes. Or... I don't know.

01:22:43.770 --> 01:22:46.930
It happened this morning, when you came to me

01:22:47.010 --> 01:22:50.580
to make a phone call to the chief because of you.

01:22:50.660 --> 01:22:53.870
What, does it seem like a dream to anyone?

01:22:53.950 --> 01:22:59.320
You're lying, Viktoria. I can't believe you. Why?

01:23:00.440 --> 01:23:02.120
What did you destroy me for?

01:23:02.680 --> 01:23:04.740
Calm down, Clara. I gave you the drops in the morning

01:23:04.820 --> 01:23:06.740
because I was told to do so.

01:23:06.820 --> 01:23:09.950
Why did you leave right away? You poured water on me.

01:23:10.330 --> 01:23:12.210
You should lie down.

01:23:12.740 --> 01:23:14.350
From whom did you buy the water?

01:23:15.040 --> 01:23:17.210
Listen, Clara, I don't want you to feel worse.

01:23:17.440 --> 01:23:18.370
Lie down!

01:23:30.350 --> 01:23:33.170
- Don't drink! - The doctor forbade you to.

01:23:33.860 --> 01:23:34.960
And you're going to listen to me?

01:23:35.410 --> 01:23:36.560
Go lie down for a moment!

01:23:37.170 --> 01:23:39.080
- Not a word! - Admit it.

01:23:39.940 --> 01:23:42.000
We're alone here. Admit you killed me.

01:23:42.210 --> 01:23:43.210
You have no proof!

01:23:44.050 --> 01:23:45.050
No one will believe you!

01:23:49.540 --> 01:23:51.150
You sick madman!

01:23:54.890 --> 01:24:00.000
Shooting birds...

01:24:00.000 --> 01:24:01.350
Toby.

01:26:08.090 --> 01:26:10.540
I'll tell you, Clara's not in a hurry.

01:26:10.540 --> 01:26:13.830
Go back to the city, she'll be waiting for you at home.

01:26:13.830 --> 01:26:16.830
If it's not on the way, we'll take a look. You go with us, please.

01:26:17.960 --> 01:26:19.720
- You don't believe me, do you? - We'll see about that later.

01:26:31.050 --> 01:26:34.200
We're making a wasteful trip. - You think so?

01:26:34.280 --> 01:26:38.110
Clara must be waiting in town. She needs help.

01:26:39.350 --> 01:26:41.720
What are you going to do there? It's almost morning.

01:26:41.800 --> 01:26:44.120
Please. - What?

01:27:14.400 --> 01:27:17.540
If Klara comes in the meantime, she'll be in the living room.

01:27:19.630 --> 01:27:25.200
This is the only room where the light is on.

01:27:25.620 --> 01:27:28.100
I forgot to turn it off when I left.

01:27:28.550 --> 01:27:30.000
Do you still think I'm drunk?

01:27:31.630 --> 01:27:33.430
I'm sorry, I had a good idea.

01:27:36.380 --> 01:27:39.990
Will you come back to town with us?

01:27:40.080 --> 01:27:45.480
No. - But that's Clara!

01:27:45.480 --> 01:27:47.880
Oh, you maid! Nothing will calm her down.

01:27:49.430 --> 01:27:51.540
She must be here somewhere.

01:28:34.540 --> 01:28:37.840
Get out of here, Clara. We'll stop playing.

01:28:39.190 --> 01:28:41.440
It's good you're locked up.

01:28:43.440 --> 01:28:45.270
At least no one will disturb us.

01:29:04.280 --> 01:29:07.330
It's really me, alive and sound.

01:29:08.020 --> 01:29:11.260
You don't have hallucinations like your sister, do you?

01:29:11.860 --> 01:29:15.260
You're quite an ordinary killer.

01:29:17.380 --> 01:29:20.860
But you can't kill me. Fortunately, I can swim.

01:29:22.940 --> 01:29:25.370
So which double the price? Do you know why?

01:29:27.610 --> 01:29:29.600
500,000 and all the spares.

01:29:33.480 --> 01:29:36.950
- You won't get anything! - Just shout it out, I don't care.

01:29:36.950 --> 01:29:44.540
Your sister doesn't know her name yet, but I don't think she should suffer in the dark for long.

01:29:44.540 --> 01:29:49.880
Tomorrow she and her friends will find out that you poisoned her.

01:29:49.880 --> 01:29:53.460
You have a long way to go until tomorrow, I'll report in the afternoon.

01:29:53.460 --> 01:29:58.450
Two attempts at murder will be enough for you.

01:30:46.350 --> 01:30:53.520
We all got lost once, depending on who's going to show us the way.

01:30:53.800 --> 01:31:00.000
And you came to find out.

01:31:00.030 --> 01:31:04.030
I'll show you. It's not a nice path.

01:31:05.760 --> 01:31:10.630
Drink, please.

01:31:11.230 --> 01:31:13.730
That's the right way to drink.

01:31:15.330 --> 01:31:20.960
It'll never hurt again.

01:31:23.140 --> 01:31:25.400
I wanted water.

01:31:27.370 --> 01:31:30.000
Water is said to be harmful.

01:31:30.000 --> 01:31:32.760
The more you talk about it, the more I feel sorry for you.

01:31:32.840 --> 01:31:35.000
Give me some more. - No, no, no, please.

01:31:35.080 --> 01:31:37.240
Give me some more. - No, I'm sick.

01:31:37.320 --> 01:31:42.420
It's a wonderful medicine, trust me.

01:31:43.040 --> 01:31:46.810
But I must die. They poisoned me, you know.

01:31:46.900 --> 01:31:50.740
Well, that's a good reason. - No, no.

01:31:50.820 --> 01:31:56.920
Give me some more.

01:32:11.130 --> 01:32:18.020
It's the best time of the year. Come on, wait for me. Wait!

01:32:19.000 --> 01:32:28.470
Sister, you know me. - You have a great sister. Come on.

01:32:30.000 --> 01:32:40.080
Come here! Don't be afraid, I won't poison you.

01:33:50.960 --> 01:33:52.340
Have you seen any girl here?

01:34:04.480 --> 01:34:07.260
We have to move on. We'll have to search the whole forest.

01:34:13.500 --> 01:34:20.520
She's dead.

01:35:08.920 --> 01:35:13.460
Clara, if you weren't a woman, I'd kill you.

01:35:15.350 --> 01:35:20.320
I'll tell the court and if you're lucky, they'll find out you're mentally ill.

01:35:21.250 --> 01:35:22.970
Only then can you be saved.

01:35:23.460 --> 01:35:30.000
You fools! If you were a soldier, I'd leave my gun to you.

01:35:30.000 --> 01:35:32.760
- She's too tired. - Tanya, let's go.

01:37:36.360 --> 01:37:39.280
Collect those pearls for me, I've run out of them.

01:37:39.280 --> 01:37:46.160
Where did you hide the cat?

01:37:46.160 --> 01:37:48.950
I don't know, I think the informant threw it in the trash.

01:39:19.390 --> 01:39:23.360
Unfortunately, Mrs. Tranganová died last night.

01:39:25.230 --> 01:39:30.000
That's not possible. The beast won't kill. - We know that.

01:39:30.990 --> 01:39:32.310
The patient is recovering.

01:39:33.410 --> 01:39:35.010
The older sister, Victoria, has died.

01:39:35.090 --> 01:39:36.020
Who's calling, please?

01:39:40.880 --> 01:39:48.370
-Madame. -Yes, sir.

01:39:51.050 --> 01:39:54.870
-Konjak, two, three. -Can I go now?

01:39:54.990 --> 01:39:58.030
The crisis has passed, your life is in danger.

01:39:58.500 --> 01:39:59.220
Be careful.

01:40:00.030 --> 01:40:04.150
- And what kind of poison was it? - That's right, it's not in the doctor's power.

01:40:05.080 --> 01:40:06.560
He called for hallucinations.

01:40:07.390 --> 01:40:10.400
There are many poisonous plants,

01:40:10.630 --> 01:40:12.510
the stinger of a fly, and so on.

01:40:13.210 --> 01:40:14.890
Various kinds of deadly poison.

01:40:16.680 --> 01:40:19.280
Even in a living person there are some poisons,

01:40:19.810 --> 01:40:23.370
for example in saliva, and they are transmitted very easily.

01:40:24.700 --> 01:40:27.140
- Maybe with a pill? - Don't make it easy for the young man.

01:40:27.320 --> 01:40:29.670
- I'm probably useless here. - A chemist.

01:40:30.220 --> 01:40:34.760
who understands food and has a little sense of equality.

01:40:34.840 --> 01:40:38.330
How is it possible that alcohol could cause such a poison?

01:40:38.580 --> 01:40:41.540
Of course, it can't.

01:40:41.660 --> 01:40:43.940
It was poisonous, above all.

01:40:44.190 --> 01:40:46.750
The poison was temporary, the alcohol only succeeded in the reaction

01:40:46.830 --> 01:40:49.900
and thus the healing, you see.

01:40:54.250 --> 01:40:55.530
Did you say something, doctor?
